  "note": "Opponent seats are parameterised archetypes, not real decklists. Each seat samples a profile from a table mix and then jitters every number, so a 500-game batch faces a spread of opponents rather than one fixed gauntlet. Damage is split: 45% of a seat's output comes at us and 55% is spread over the other seats, which is what lets a pod soften itself up. Three power-tier profiles (starter-precon/upgraded-casual/tuned-bracket3) set overall competence; six archetype profiles (combo/stax/aristocrats/voltron/tokens/group-hug) set the SHAPE of that pressure, each tuned distinctly rather than as a rescaled power level. wipeVulnerability scales how hard one of our board wipes cuts a seat's output — a wipe barely slows a combo or stax deck (no board to lose) and guts a token board.",
